## Context

Child of tracking ticket 0252. The audit
(docs/audit-0252-worktree-ownership-2026-07-12.md) found gaze creates its
review worktrees under `/tmp/review-<pr>`, outside the `.claude/worktrees/`
fast-path every guard keys on — so neither the existing guards nor the new
0296 identity guard cover them. Both audit incidents are uncovered there.

## Relevant files

- `skills/gaze/SKILL.md` — review-worktree creation site
- `scripts/guard-*.sh`, `scripts/pretooluse-worktree-path-guard.sh` — fast-path patterns
- 0296's new guard — must cover whichever location wins

## Actions

1. Decide: move gaze review worktrees under `<repo>/.claude/worktrees/review-<pr>`
   (preferred — one guarded namespace), or broaden every guard's fast-path
   to include the /tmp pattern.
2. Apply the choice; sweep for other skills creating worktrees outside
   `.claude/worktrees/` (verify forks were known to use /tmp too).
3. Update cleanup paths (worktree-gc, stale-worktree checks) for the new location.

## Test

- Replay a mutation inside a gaze review worktree and assert the 0296
  guard evaluates it (not fast-pathed to silence).

## Verification

- [ ] No harness skill creates worktrees outside the guarded namespace(s)
- [ ] gaze end-to-end still works (review worktree created, used, cleaned)

## Invariants

- gaze behavior unchanged apart from the worktree location

## Exit criteria

- [ ] All skill-created worktrees live inside guard coverage
- [ ] `make check` passes
